{"task_id": "HumanEval/10", "solution": "def make_palindrome(string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\" Find the shortest palindrome that begins with a supplied string.\n    Algorithm idea is simple:\n    - Find the longest postfix of supplied string that is a palindrome.\n    - Append to the end of the string reverse of a string prefix that comes before the palindromic suffix.\n    >>> make_palindrome('')\n    ''\n    >>> make_palindrome('cat')\n    'catac'\n    >>> make_palindrome('cata')\n    'catac'\n    \"\"\"\n    if not string:\n        return \"\"\n\n    n = len(string)\n    # Iterate to find the longest palindromic suffix.\n    # The first i for which string[i:] is a palindrome will be the longest suffix\n    # because we check suffixes starting from the beginning of the string.\n    for i in range(n):\n        suffix = string[i:]\n        if is_palindrome(suffix):\n            # The part to append is the reverse of the prefix before this palindromic suffix.\n            prefix_to_reverse = string[:i]\n            return string + prefix_to_reverse[::-1]\n\n    # This point should theoretically not be reached because at least a single-character suffix (string[n-1:])\n    # is always a palindrome.\n    return string"}
