{"task_id": "HumanEval/24", "solution": "def largest_divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\" For a given number n, find the largest number that divides n evenly, smaller than n.\n    This function efficiently finds the largest proper divisor by checking factors up to sqrt(n).\n    \"\"\"\n    largest_proper_divisor = 1\n\n    # Iterate from 2 up to the square root of n to find divisors.\n    # We only need to check up to sqrt(n) because if i divides n, then n/i also divides n.\n    # One of i or n/i will be <= sqrt(n) and the other >= sqrt(n).\n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            # i is a divisor. Since i >= 2, i is a proper divisor.\n            largest_proper_divisor = max(largest_proper_divisor, i)\n\n            # n // i is also a divisor. Since i >= 2, n // i will be smaller than n.\n            # This is often the larger proper divisor.\n            largest_proper_divisor = max(largest_proper_divisor, n // i)\n\n    return largest_proper_divisor"}
