{"task_id": "HumanEval/32", "solution": "import math\n\n\ndef poly(xs: list, x: float):\n    \"\"\"\n    Evaluates polynomial with coefficients xs at point x.\n    return xs[0] + xs[1] * x + xs[1] * x^2 + .... xs[n] * x^n\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum([coeff * math.pow(x, i) for i, coeff in enumerate(xs)])\n\n\ndef find_zero(xs: list):\n    \"\"\" xs are coefficients of a polynomial.\n    find_zero find x such that poly(x) = 0.\n    find_zero returns only only zero point, even if there are many.\n    Moreover, find_zero only takes list xs having even number of coefficients\n    and largest non zero coefficient as it guarantees\n    a solution.\n    >>> round(find_zero([1, 2]), 2) # f(x) = 1 + 2x\n    -0.5\n    >>> round(find_zero([-6, 11, -6, 1]), 2) # (x - 1) * (x - 2) * (x - 3) = -6 + 11x - 6x^2 + x^3\n    1.0\n    \"\"\"\n    DEFAULT_TOL = 1e-12  # Tolerance for root convergence\n    DEFAULT_COMPLEX_REAL_TOL = 1e-10  # Tolerance to consider complex number \"real\"\n    DEFAULT_MAX_ITER = 1000  # Maximum iterations for Durand-Kerner\n\n    degree = len(xs) - 1\n    # Problem statement guarantees degree >= 1 and odd, so a real root exists.\n\n    # Helper for convergence check\n    def _is_close(a: complex, b: complex, tol: float) -> bool:\n        return abs(a - b) < tol\n\n    # Generate initial guesses (scaled roots of unity)\n    roots = []\n    if degree > 0:\n        radius = 0.5 + degree\n        for k in range(degree):\n            angle = 2 * math.pi * k / degree\n            roots.append(radius * complex(math.cos(angle), math.sin(angle)))\n    else:\n        # Should not be reached based on problem constraints\n        return float(-xs[0]) if xs[0] != 0 else 0.0 # Fallback for constant polynomial, though problem implies degree > 0.\n\n    # Durand-Kerner iteration\n    leading_coeff = xs[degree]\n    for _ in range(DEFAULT_MAX_ITER):\n        new_roots = list(roots)\n        converged_all = True\n\n        for i, z_i in enumerate(roots):\n            p_val = poly(xs, z_i)\n\n            # If poly(z_i) is already near zero, z_i is a good root guess.\n            if abs(p_val) < DEFAULT_TOL:\n                new_roots[i] = z_i\n                continue\n\n            # Calculate product for the denominator: product_{j != i} (z_i - z_j)\n            denominator = complex(1.0, 0.0)\n            for j, z_j in enumerate(roots):\n                if i != j:\n                    diff = z_i - z_j\n                    if abs(diff) < DEFAULT_TOL:\n                        # Roots are too close, denominator would be problematic.\n                        # Keep the old root for stability in this iteration.\n                        denominator = complex(0.0, 0.0)\n                        break\n                    denominator *= diff\n\n            if abs(denominator) < DEFAULT_TOL:\n                # If denominator is problematic (near zero), skip update for this root.\n                new_roots[i] = z_i\n            else:\n                # Update rule for non-monic polynomials: P_monic(z_i) = P(z_i) / leading_coeff\n                updated_z_i = z_i - (p_val / leading_coeff) / denominator\n                new_roots[i] = updated_z_i\n\n            # Check convergence for this root\n            if not _is_close(z_i, new_roots[i], DEFAULT_TOL):\n                converged_all = False\n\n        roots = new_roots\n\n        if converged_all:\n            break\n\n    # Select the first real root that meets the tolerance\n    real_candidate_roots = []\n    for r in roots:\n        if abs(r.imag) < DEFAULT_COMPLEX_REAL_TOL:\n            real_candidate_roots.append(r.real)\n\n    # Sort to pick the smallest magnitude real root if multiple are found,\n    # consistent with docstring examples (1.0 for cubic, -0.5 for linear).\n    if real_candidate_roots:\n        real_candidate_roots.sort(key=lambda x: abs(x))\n        return real_candidate_roots[0]\n    else:\n        # This branch should ideally not be reached due to problem statement's guarantee.\n        # As a fallback, return the real part of the first root found.\n        return roots[0].real"}
