{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th Fib4 number iteratively.\n    This function avoids recursion for efficient computation using a sliding window.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize a, b, c, d as fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3) respectively\n    a, b, c, d = 0, 0, 2, 0\n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        # Calculate the next Fib4 number\n        next_fib4 = a + b + c + d\n        # Shift the window: a becomes b, b becomes c, c becomes d, d becomes next_fib4\n        a, b, c, d = b, c, d, next_fib4\n    \n    return d"}
