{"task_id": "HumanEval/62", "solution": "def derivative(xs: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the derivative of a polynomial represented by a list of coefficients.\n    The input list xs[i] represents the coefficient of x^i.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not xs or len(xs) == 1:\n        return []\n\n    # The derivative of c * x^i is i * c * x^(i-1).\n    # The constant term (i=0) vanishes.\n    # The new coefficients are for x^0, x^1, x^2, ...\n    return [i * coeff for i, coeff in enumerate(xs) if i > 0]"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/62", "solution": "def derivative(xs: list):\n    \"\"\" xs represent coefficients of a polynomial.\n    Returns the coefficients of the derivative of the polynomial.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(xs) <= 1:\n        return []\n    \n    # new_coeffs[k] = (k+1) * xs[k+1] for k from 0 to len(xs)-2\n    # This corresponds to i * xs[i] for i from 1 to len(xs)-1\n    return [i * xs[i] for i in range(1, len(xs))]"}
