{"task_id": "HumanEval/163", "solution": "def generate_integers(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given two positive integers a and b, return the even digits between a\n    and b, in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_val = min(a, b)\n    max_val = max(a, b)\n    \n    # \"Even digits\" are defined as single-digit even integers: 0, 2, 4, 6, 8.\n    allowed_digits = {0, 2, 4, 6, 8}\n    \n    result = []\n    for digit in sorted(allowed_digits):\n        if min_val <= digit <= max_val:\n            result.append(digit)\n            \n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/163", "solution": "def generate_integers(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given two positive integers a and b, return the even digits between a\n    and b, in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_val = min(a, b)\n    max_val = max(a, b)\n\n    # Find the first even number in the range [min_val, max_val]\n    first_even = min_val if min_val % 2 == 0 else min_val + 1\n\n    # If the first even number is greater than max_val, there are no even numbers in the range\n    if first_even > max_val:\n        return []\n\n    # Generate the list of even numbers\n    return list(range(first_even, max_val + 1, 2))"}
